title: Microsoft Intune: App Licenses
agents: special
catalog: cloud/microsoft
license: GPLv2
distribution: Christopher Pommer
description:
 This check monitors license consumption for applications published through
 Microsoft Intune. Microsoft Intune manages mobile applications and can distribute
 licensed apps from various sources including the iOS Volume Purchase Program (VPP).

 The check processes data collected by the {Microsoft Intune} special agent, which
 queries the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve license information for all published
 applications in the Intune tenant.

 License monitoring tracks consumption and availability with configurable thresholds:

 - {Absolute thresholds}: Alert when available licenses fall below specific numbers

 - {Percentage thresholds}: Alert when available licenses fall below specific percentages

 - {Minimum license threshold}: Only monitor apps with at least a specified number of total licenses

 The service displays consumption percentage, used and available license counts.
 Performance metrics are provided for tracking license usage trends over time.

 Service states are configurable based on available license thresholds. 
 Default mapping:

 {OK}: Available licenses below minimum monitoring threshold

 {WARN}: Available licenses below warning threshold (default: 10% remaining)

 {CRIT}: Available licenses below critical threshold (default: 5% remaining)

 The service details include application publisher, type, total licenses, consumption
 status, and assignment information.

 You must configure the {Microsoft Intune} special agent to collect application
 license data from your Intune tenant.

item:
 The application name combined with the app type, formatted as "{app_name} - {app_type}".
 For example, app types include "iOS VPP" for iOS Volume Purchase Program apps.

discovery:
 One service is created automatically for each published application found in the
 Intune tenant. Services are named "Intune app {app_name} - {app_type}" where
 both the application name and distribution type are included for unique identification.